---
/**
 * Elfsight floating reviews badge — sitewide.
 *
 * POSITIONING IS CONFIGURED IN ELFSIGHT, NOT HERE. Deliberately.
 *
 * Elfsight exposes separate mobile and desktop settings for the badge, so the
 * clearance above the sticky call bar is set in their editor on the mobile
 * layout. That is why this component is a bare div: there is no CSS override
 * and no script.
 *
 * DO NOT reintroduce a CSS or JS override for the badge's offset. An earlier
 * attempt forced `bottom: <clearance> !important` onto the widget, and the
 * consequence is worse than the original problem — it silently overrides
 * whatever is configured in Elfsight, so changing the offset in their editor
 * appears to do nothing and the next person debugs the dashboard for an hour.
 *
 * Two facts worth keeping, since both cost time to establish:
 *
 *   - The widget mounts into `attachShadow({ mode: 'open' })`. Shadow DOM
 *     encapsulates styles, so an external stylesheet cannot reach it at all,
 *     no matter how the selector is written. Anything that appears to work from
 *     the outside is acting on a light-DOM wrapper, not the badge.
 *   - Its class names come from styled-components and are build hashes that
 *     change between releases, so they were never a stable hook either.
 *
 * Between those two, every in-code route to moving this badge is either
 * impossible or fragile. The vendor setting is the correct place, and it exists.
 */
---

<div class="elfsight-app-b264d3c7-506f-49e7-989e-31b7555fa5b1" data-elfsight-app-lazy></div>
